{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgYgJ7j3J6va3Yd94Yuf6","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Frontend** code runs on the user's device, usually in the browser or a mobile app. It handles what the user sees and interacts with:\n- Rendering the UI: layout, styling, components\n- Handling input such as clicks, forms and gestures\n- Managing client-side state, routing and loading, empty and error states\n- Calling backend APIs and showing the results\n- Typical tech: HTML, CSS, JavaScript/TypeScript, React, Vue, Swift or Kotlin for mobile\n\n**Backend** code runs on servers you control. It handles data, rules and anything that must be trusted:\n- Business logic and validation\n- Authentication and authorization (who can do what)\n- Reading and writing databases, running migrations\n- Talking to other systems (payments, email, third-party APIs) and running background jobs\n- Exposing APIs, such as REST or GraphQL, for the frontend to call\n- Typical tech: Node.js, Python, Java, Go, C#, plus databases like PostgreSQL\n\n**The key difference is trust.** Users can inspect and change frontend code, so it can't be relied on for security. Client-side validation only gives the user faster feedback. The backend has to enforce permissions, validate input again and protect secrets like API keys and database credentials.\n\n**How they connect:** the frontend sends HTTP requests to the backend's API. The backend checks the request, applies the rules, reads or writes data and sends back a response, often JSON. The frontend then displays it.\n\n**Gray areas:**\n- Server-side rendering (Next.js, Rails views): code on the server produces the UI.\n- \"Backend-for-frontend\" layers: thin server code shaped for one particular client.\n- \"Full-stack\" means working across both.\n\nA rough rule: if code decides what the user sees or how it feels, it's frontend. If it decides what's true, what's allowed or what gets stored, it's backend."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":12859,"cache_read_input_tokens":29564,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":12859},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1071fdae-73e9-4cda-838e-d34491f052b1","uuid":"3c24b078-38dc-4f12-ae21-c53505fe6df4","timestamp":"2026-10-30T15:43:43.899Z","request_id":"req_011CgYgJ7PhrUzyRsJTSqdZi"}
